WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.860
Tesla is preparing to showcase its dedicated semi-factory on September 24 after years of pilot production. This is Tesla Shorts Time, episode 603. Tesla has begun sending invites for the September 24th event focused on the dedicated commercial truck factory. The gathering follows years of pilot runs and gradual manufacturing ramp. Invites are being sent to media and select fleet customers. The event is expected to cover production scaling plans for

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:54.900
fleet customers. The semi-program is positioned to unlock software revenue opportunities estimated at $17 billion. The European semi will launch in 2027 with camera mirrors, different lighting, and a 550-kilometer range. It carries a 40-ton combined weight limit and charges at 800 kilowatts, recovering up to 60% of range in 30 minutes.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:01:10.940
The tractor weighs 9.1 tons. Europe receives one announced version rather than the US standard and long range split. The changes balance battery weight against mandatory driver break times that allow recharging instead of carrying larger packs.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:21.400
Tesla is building the largest grid battery in the United States at XAI Memphis site. The project pairs Tesla Energy Storage with the AI Compute Campus.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:31.400
The installation supports continuous power needs for large-scale AI training clusters. The Model 3 production line in a gigafactory Shanghai is running at full capacity.

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:43.940
Weight times for long-range and performance trims in China have moved to 6-8 weeks. The new 176 kilowatt TL2 front motor upgrade is now rolling onto the line.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:52.460
Supply chain reports confirm the motor change is active in current builds. No timeline was given for when the upgrade reaches other markets.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:02:03.780
Tesla China growth streak reached double digits for the latest period. The pace remains modest compared with prior years. The streak follows several quarters of slower growth in the market.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:15.020
Tesla Electric is offering two power walls on a $35 monthly lease in Texas. The program targets residential customers seeking storage without large upfront costs.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:21.660
The lease covers equipment and basic installation. Availability is currently limited to the Texas market.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:33.320
Tesla FSD drove the editor 2.5 hours to the flight 93 memorial. The trip allowed time on site for the 25th anniversary honoring the 40 heroes aboard the flight.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:45.180
The editor posted about the experience on X with photos from the memorial grounds. The journey highlighted the supervised FSD system's ability to handle a long highway route without intervention.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:57.900
Ashok Elluswami shared details on the next major neural network upgrade expected later this year or early next year. The update focuses on further improvements to the supervised FSD stack.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:12.940
The version follows the V14 series now in testing. One congressman is calling on NHTSA to investigate continued misuse of Tesla full self-driving software after video evidence showed 43 drivers sleep at the wheel.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:22.500
The request highlights ongoing concerns about driver engagement and system safeguards. The videos were compiled and shared publicly before the lawmaker letter.

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:34.460
Tesla has not yet issued a public response to the specific demand. Tesla conducted a Robotaxi demonstration in Japan. The event marks the first public showing of the vehicle in that market.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:42.620
The demonstration follows similar showings in other regions earlier this year. No timeline for commercial operations in Japan was announced.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:55.560
Multiple recent US sightings of cybercabs occurred, including in Washington, Florida, New York, and Texas. Two cybercabs were parked near a Tesla supercharger close to a resident home in Samamish, Washington.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:04:07.120
A cybercab was observed on the 192 near Disney World on September 10. A cybercab was seen on the cross island expressway with a driver behind the wheel in the New York area.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:17.720
The Oasis supercharger location handled 6,038 charging sessions over the Labor Day weekend. The site demonstrated high utilization during peak travel periods.

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:33.960
The location serves both Tesla and non-Tesla vehicles under the open access policy. Utility scale battery projects tied directly to AI training campuses introduce a new demand pattern that differs from traditional grid balancing or renewable smoothing.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:43.240
The Memphis installation for XAI shows storage size to match continuous high draw compute loads rather than daily solar or wind cycles.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:50.120
This changes the utilization math because the battery must support steady draw instead of short peak shaving events.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:58.160
The economics shift when the customer is an internal or affiliated compute operator rather than a utility under rate base rules.

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:05.920
Capital recovery can occur through avoided grid charges or through internal transfer pricing that does not require public rate cases.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:17.840
Over multiple sites, the pattern could accelerate factory output targets for mega pack lines, while also exposing the business to concentration risk if a few large AI customers dominate the backlog.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:27.700
Before we go, the September 24 semi event may clarify production timelines for fleet customers. And that's everything worth knowing about Tesla today.

